---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_79",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 79,
  "text": "<p> [[327.2]] <b>80. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS</p>\n<p> [[327.3]] Hannover, 27. Juni (7. Juli) 1690. [49.81.]</b></p>\n<p> [[327.16]] Hanoverae 27 Jun. 1690 </p>\n<p> [[327.17]] Nobilissime et Consultissime Vir, Fautor Honoratissime </p>\n<p> [[327.18]] Si unquam nunc certe sub initium literarum hac vulgari formula uti possum: <i>Si vales bene\n[[327.19]] est, ego quidem valeo</i>. Nam per biennium et amplius domo abfui, per magnam Germaniae\n[[327.20]] Italiaeque partem divagatus, idque jussu principis mei, et inquirendis Historiarum monumentis\n[[327.21]] circa majores Serenissimae Gentis, supplendisque Archivorum nostrorum hiatibus. Nec sane\n[[327.22]] pauca ex Suevia et Bavaria, sed maxime ex Italia attuli, quibus Guelfica illustrantur, et\n[[327.23]] connexio Brunsvicensis Estensisque Familiarum a scriptoribus male tradita ex diplomatibus\n[[327.24]] corrigitur et in clara luce collocatur. Nunc Deo favente reversus veteres necessitudines resumo;\n[[327.25]] <b>teque inter primos compello, cujus et doctrinam et candorem semper\n[[328.1]] maximi feci</b>. Spero Te valetudine optata frui, contigisse enim mutationem in melius magna\n[[328.2]] mea voluptate vidi ex compellatione publica qua Magliabecchium aliosque amicos ad symbolam\n[[328.3]] conferendam venationi larvatorum scriptorum tuae invitas. Hanc primus mihi Florentiae\n[[328.4]] ostendit Magliabecchius. Dixi non satis sibi cavisse, dum enim mihi has tuas literas communicaret,\n[[328.5]] eo ipso me procuratorem rerum tuarum fecisse contra semet; <b>jamque</b> <b>muneris esse\n[[328.6]] mei urgere, insistere, opportune, importune,</b> ut mecum aliquid auferre possem ab\n[[328.7]] ipso in usus Tuos. Sed nihil egi, etsi enim vir sit maximae lectionis; mirifice tamen distrahitur\n[[328.8]] tum compellationibus amicorum domi suae, tum vero maxime Epistolis, quibus tantum non\n[[328.9]] obruitur. Interim Vintimigliae specimen ipso suasore editum, acceperis. Hortatus sum deinde,\n[[328.10]] ut eruditos sibi notos ex variis ordinibus religiosis excitet ad communem operam, id enim saepe\n[[328.11]] ad ipsorum ordinum dignitatem laudemve pertinere. Et aderat forte <b>Dominicanus aliquis\n[[328.12]] vir doctus,</b> qui non videbatur ab hac cogitatione alienus. Videbo an aliquid produxerit mea\n[[328.13]] suasio. </p>\n<p> [[328.14]] Tu vero, inquies, alios hortaris, dum ipse desideriis meis dees. Mihi vero fateor, <i>curta</i> <i>est\n[[328.15]] supellex</i> et pleraque quae in hoc genere noveram, tibi dudum explorata non dubito. Si qua sunt\n[[328.16]] minus pervulgata, ea non occurrunt, distracto tot aliis cogitationibus. Hoc ipso momento, dum\n[[328.17]] quaedam in Schedis meis revolvo, video annotasse me aliquando sequentia: 1. <i>Trattato del\n[[328.18]] titolo regio dovuto alla serenissima casa di Savoia in Torino 1633. fol.</i> Exemplo quod vidi\n[[328.19]] ascripta erant haec verba: <i>Ill^#'m^#'o Viro Claudio Expilli in Senatu Gratianopolitano Praesidi\n[[328.20]] amplissimo <b>Petrus Monodus</b> Commentarioli hujus autor</i> <i>amicitiae observantiaeque suae</b>\n[[328.21]] <i>monimentum D. M.</i> </p>\n<p> [[329.1]] Hujusmodi alia fortasse nonnulla latent vel in schedis meis, vel in mente, sed ut dixi, non\n[[329.2]] statim jussa comparent. </p>\n<p> [[329.3]] 2. <b>Basilii Valentini</b> nomen esse fictitium et a duobus effectibus primariis lapidis\n[[329.4]] philosophorum jactati sumtum divitiis regiis, et perfecta valetudine, dudum suspicatus sum, et\n[[329.5]] Cl^#'m^#'o <b>Tollio</b> sententiam meam Viennae aperui, qui ab ea non videbatur abhorrere, idque nuper\n[[329.6]] indicavit in libello edito, titulo <i>Sapientiae insanientis</i>. Nescio an Rudolphus Imperator ut narrat\n[[329.7]] Tollius, in Monachi hujus crediti res inquisierit, illud scio Philippum Electorem Moguntinum\n[[329.8]] Erfordia potitum investigari jussisse apud Benedictinos ejus civitatis sed frustra. Ego ut verum\n[[329.9]] fatear, dubito an scriptor sit tam antiquus, qui ut ipse videri vult libros suos composuerit eo\n[[329.10]] tempore quo lues venerea innotuit; dictio enim Germanica recentius aliquid spirat, nisi dicere\n[[329.11]] malimus fuisse scripta Basilii a Joh. Tholdio interpolata. Hic enim quorundam editor habetur.\n[[329.12]] Et sunt qui credunt Tholdium cognatione junctum autori, quaedam ex ejus schedis in <i>Haligraphiam</i>\n[[329.13]] suam transtulisse. </p>\n<p> [[329.14]] Non dubito quin noveris, duorum librorum Gallicorum quibus tituli: <i>l'art de penser</i>; et\n[[329.15]] <i>nouveaux Elemens de Geometrie</i>; autorem esse <b>Ant. Arnaldum</b>. Res certa est, quoniam\n[[329.16]] didici ex ipsomet olim Parisiis. Sed alterius libri itidem Parisiis editi hoc titulo: <i>Elemens de\n[[329.17]] Mathematique Universelle</i>, in 4^#'o, autor est <b>Joh. Prestet</b>, qui laborem illum Malebranchii\n[[329.18]] auspiciis suscepit; notus mihi erat uterque cum Parisiis versarer. </p>\n<p> [[330.1]] Nescio an non noris dudum annotarisque, autorem libri pro Danis contra Suecos sub\n[[330.2]] Carolo Gustavo hostes scripti, qui se vocat <b>Orosium Annilonem</b>, fuisse <b>Vitum Beringium</b>. </p>\n<p> [[330.4]] Hortatu Boineburgii in Polonia legationem pro Neoburgico obituri libellum nomine\n[[330.5]] <b>Georgii Ulicovii</b> Lithuani scripsit G. G. L., ubi autor positis certis definitionibus pene ad\n[[330.6]] demonstrationis formam ostendere conatus est, quid tunc esset consultum ei Reipublicae.\n[[330.7]] Boeclerus qui editum libellum a Boineburgio acceperat, eo valde delectabatur, ejusque in\n[[330.8]] libello quodam posthumo meminit tanquam sine exemplo exquisiti. Exemplar ejus nullum\n[[330.9]] habeo jam a multis annis. Sed quid te his minutiis teneo? </p>\n<p> [[330.10]] Apud Dn. Horbium (insignem apud vos verbi divini ministrum) biennio abhinc agebat\n[[330.11]] eruditus quidam juvenis Medicus nomine <b>Stahl</b>, qui liberos Horbii ni fallor informabat. Is\n[[330.12]] mihi solebat quaedam interdum significare nova et curiosa in illo quod colebat studiorum\n[[330.13]] genere. Quaeso fac mihi hanc gratiam et inquire quorsum devenerit, et si vacat significa.\n[[330.14]] Celeberrimum <b>Morhofium</b> non dubito progredi in praeclaro opere <i>Polyhistoris</b>, si essem ipsi\n[[330.15]] vicinior lubentissime cum eo aliquando cogitata conferrem. Sed haec per intervallum commode\n[[330.16]] non fiunt. </p>\n<p> [[330.17]] Ante omnia nosse velim quo sint loco tua <i>Ethicae Elementa</i>, <b>quorum consilio valde\n[[330.18]] applaudo,</b> quaeque alia nunc pares Te non minus quam publico digna et quid alioqui res\n[[330.19]] literaria ferat novi.\n [[330.20]] /  Vale et fave Fautor eximie cultori obsequentissimo Gothofredo Guilielmo Leibnitio </p>\n<p> [[331.1]] P. S. Nuper habui in manibus <b>indicem quorundam librorum larvatorum scriptorum\n[[331.2]] a Jesuitis, circa annum 1630 jam confectum, quem nescio unde\n[[331.3]] descriptum inter schedas meas repereram. Sed nunc dum mittere volo, non\n[[331.4]] comparet.</b> Redibit sub oculos haud dubie, nec tardabo eum ad te destinare. </p>\n",
  "number": "80.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS",
  "date": "Hannover, 27. Juni (7. Juli) 1690. [49.81.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:80. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS Hannover, 27. Juni (7. Juli) 1690. [49.81.] Hanoverae 27 Jun. 1690 Nobilissime et Consultissime Vir, Fautor Honoratissime Si unquam nunc certe sub initium literarum hac vulgari formula uti possum: Si vales bene est, ego quidem valeo. Nam per biennium et amplius domo a...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>